    "narrative": "The centerpiece of today\u2019s lineup is **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, who boasts an elite 81.89 efficiency score against Hughes. With a favorable park factor and a premium spot in the three-hole, he is our clear priority for production. Following closely is **Bryce Harper**, scoring a robust 74.91; despite a slight platoon disadvantage against the lefty Mathews, his elite xwOBA and favorable park environment make him a must-start anchor. **Jonathan Aranda** and **Lawrence Butler** also offer significant value today, both benefiting from dynamic platoon advantages and high-leverage order positioning that pushes their scores well into the 70s.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision was excluding **Gavin Sheets**, who was the strongest consideration for a bench spot at 45.80. While he offers a positive platoon edge against Kremer, his lower SP skill matchup and weaker park factors kept him behind **Zack Gelof** and **Jung Hoo Lee**. Elsewhere, we are leaning heavily into the matchup against Lopez; both **Yainer Diaz** and **Daulton Varsho** are buoyed by strong BvP historical data (26 PA) and the favorable 4.92 xERA of the opposing starter, providing a combined floor that is difficult to ignore despite some platoon-based volatility for **Daulton Varsho**.\n\nRisk management remains a priority today, as several starters are facing high-skill arms that threaten to suppress run totals. **Gleyber Torres** is our most marginal start at 47.77, hampered by a significant platoon disadvantage and unfavorable BvP history. We are effectively betting on his talent to outweigh the statistical resistance of the Wacha matchup. As we monitor the board, ensure no late-breaking weather patterns emerge, but otherwise, the lineup is optimized to maximize efficiency in the high-scarcity SB category while capitalizing on the projected weakness of today's opposing rotation.",
